// An array as a value, methods, kept (a loop): `method bool g() { for (int j = 0; j < 2; j++) { x += 1 } return a }
// initial state A do y = g() go to A`. KIELER rejects it: returning ‘int *’ from a function with return type ‘char’
// makes integer from pointer without a cast [-Wint-conversion].
scchart Main { input bool b input int i int a[2] = {4,7} int c[2] = {4,7} int m[2][2] = {{4,7},{8,1}} float fa[2] bool ba[2] output int x output float f output bool y method bool g() { for (int j = 0; j < 2; j++) { x += 1 } return a } initial state A do y = g() go to A }
